{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family sized dwellinghouse.&nbsp;This would be detrimental to the borough&#39;s stock of family-sized dwellinghouses, the need for which is set out in the development plan and supporting evidence.&nbsp;The provision of two smaller flats is not considered sufficient to justify this, particularly noting that there would be no increase in bedrooms and the flats would not provide a high quality of accommodation. The harm caused by way of a reduction in the borough&#39;s supply of family sized dwellinghouses significantly and demonstrably outweighs the benefits of the proposed flats.&nbsp;As such, the proposal would conflict with the following policies which seek to ensure that the borough&#39;s housing supply meets the needs of its residents:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D6, H1, H2, H9 &amp; H10 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policies SPDG 1 &amp; SP3 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
